From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:18:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 250/342] usb_raw: control requests without data may come
 without a buffer

A request with no data stage (SET_FEATURE, CLEAR_FEATURE) sent through
BUSBDevice::ControlTransfer(..., 0, NULL) failed: the driver checked
the NULL buffer for a userland address before looking at the length,
and the kit reported a general error. Found driving a hub's port
features from tools/probes/usbport.cpp (the port's project).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/bus/usb/usb_raw.cpp | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/bus/usb/usb_raw.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/bus/usb/usb_raw.cpp
index 08baebb1f9..4b3683270b 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/bus/usb/usb_raw.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/bus/usb/usb_raw.cpp
@@ -868,11 +868,15 @@ usb_raw_ioctl(void *cookie, uint32 op, void *buffer, size_t length)
 				return B_NO_MEMORY;
 			MemoryDeleter dataDeleter(controlData);
 
+			// a request without data (SET_FEATURE, ...) may come with no
+			// buffer at all: BUSBDevice::ControlTransfer(..., 0, NULL)
 			bool inTransfer = (command.control.request_type
 				& USB_ENDPOINT_ADDR_DIR_IN) != 0;
-			if (!IS_USER_ADDRESS(command.control.data)
-				|| (!inTransfer && user_memcpy(controlData,
-					command.control.data, command.control.length) != B_OK)) {
+			if ((command.control.length > 0
+					&& !IS_USER_ADDRESS(command.control.data))
+				|| (!inTransfer && command.control.length > 0
+					&& user_memcpy(controlData, command.control.data,
+						command.control.length) != B_OK)) {
 				return B_BAD_ADDRESS;
 			}
 
@@ -900,8 +904,9 @@ usb_raw_ioctl(void *cookie, uint32 op, void *buffer, size_t length)
 
 			if (command.control.status == B_OK)
 				status = B_OK;
-			if (inTransfer && user_memcpy(command.control.data, controlData,
-				command.control.length) != B_OK) {
+			if (inTransfer && command.control.length > 0
+				&& user_memcpy(command.control.data, controlData,
+					command.control.length) != B_OK) {
 				status = B_BAD_ADDRESS;
 			}
 			break;
